        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c4bc1f9e-136f-5327-99f6-6dbf847e0197",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Gerstein, Rudolf Höss, Rainer Höss\n- Organizations: Waffen-SS, SS, Degesch\n- Places: Auschwitz, Stuttgart\n- Roles: Obersturmführer, Head of Technical Disinfection Services, Obersturmbannführer, commandant\n- Products: Zyklon B\n- Documents: Gerstein Report\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Höss was born on 25 November 1901.\n- In World War II, Rudolf Höss was a Nazi German SS-Obersturmbannführer and the longest-serving commandant of Auschwitz concentration and extermination camp.\n- In 1945, Kurt Gerstein wrote the Gerstein Report.\n- Kurt Gerstein was an Obersturmführer of the Waffen-SS and became the Head of Technical Disinfection Services of the SS.\n- In that SS role, Kurt Gerstein supplied hydrogen cyanide, Zyklon B, from Degesch to Rudolf Höss in Auschwitz and conducted negotiations with the owners.\n- Rudolf Höss died on 16 April 1947.\n- Rainer Höss was born on 25 May 1965 in Stuttgart.\n- Rainer Höss is the grandson of Rudolf Höss.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "891a0c53-f051-5c06-bc70-530eeb3e4c14",
        "text": "Page: Gerstein Report. Sentence: The Gerstein Report was written in 1945 by Kurt Gerstein, an Obersturmführer (First Lieutenant) of the Waffen-SS who rose to become the Head of Technical Disinfection Services of the SS, and in that capacity supplied hydrogen cyanide (Zyklon B) from Degesch (\"Deutsche Gesellschaft für Schädlingsbekämpfung\") to Rudolf Höss in Auschwitz and conducted the negotiations with the owners.\nPage: Rudolf Höss. Sentence: Rudolf Höss (also Höß, Hoeß or Hoess; 25 November 1901 – 16 April 1947) was a Nazi German \"SS\"-\"Obersturmbannführer\" (lieutenant colonel) and the longest-serving commandant of Auschwitz concentration and extermination camp in World War II.\nPage: Rainer Höss. Sentence: Rainer Höss, born 25 May 1965 in Stuttgart, is the grandson of Rudolf Höss.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
